toggle-tool-activity-in-compact-transcript

Lane: frontend

Unit: toggle-tool-visibility-in-compact-transcript

ChildPatch: toggle-tool-activity-in-compact-transcript

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Keep the compact TUI conversation focused while retaining complete tool activity for transcript inspection and search.

Requires: none

Provides: Hide agent tool activity by default in the owned compact transcript, toggle it with Alt-o, and report visibility in the passive footer. Preserve complete detailed and searchable source, live activity and manual disclosure semantics, user shell output, warnings and startup diagnostics. Reuse retained warning cells for visible rows and warning details, and preserve applicable composer hints.

Boundary: Own compact visibility projection, tool-cell classification, passive footer integration and warning visibility. Do not change tool execution, persisted transcript data, non-owned presentation, warning source identity or other shortcuts. Presentation changes release selection, native copy mode and held layouts without deleting source.

Verification: Focused Alt-o and full-transcript integration, tool source classification, hidden-row search, layout release, footer priority, startup/runtime warning deduplication, status refresh/reflow and source-preserving copy tests.


